00:35:12.250 --> 00:35:16.270
You showed how to deploy API
and Shiny apps based on R.

00:35:16.270 --> 00:35:19.210
How does it work when
several customers call

00:35:19.210 --> 00:35:21.300
the service at the same time?

00:35:21.300 --> 00:35:22.450
Do add pods?

00:35:22.450 --> 00:35:24.920
You manage to have them call in?

00:35:24.920 --> 00:35:27.530
I want to make sure I
understand your question.

00:35:27.530 --> 00:35:31.240
So when you deploy a
Shiny app or an API,

00:35:31.240 --> 00:35:36.070
RStudio Server Pro is
going to create a bundle

00:35:36.070 --> 00:35:39.310
and ship that over
to RStudio Connect.

00:35:39.310 --> 00:35:44.080
So RStudio Connect can
handle multiple bundles

00:35:44.080 --> 00:35:45.400
simultaneously.

00:35:45.400 --> 00:35:47.960
So it can handle all these
bundles coming into it.

00:35:47.960 --> 00:35:51.350
And then when it rebuilds
that application,

00:35:51.350 --> 00:35:56.800
it's going to create a container
inside of RStudio Connect

00:35:56.800 --> 00:35:59.410
to run that application.

00:35:59.410 --> 00:36:02.360
So every bundle is going to
get a different container.

00:36:02.360 --> 00:36:06.010
And that's what you
can kind of see here

00:36:06.010 --> 00:36:07.650
with the source versions.

00:36:07.650 --> 00:36:10.760
Let me pull up the other one.

00:36:10.760 --> 00:36:13.810
Where's the documents?

00:36:13.810 --> 00:36:18.550
If I come here, you can
see different versions

00:36:18.550 --> 00:36:20.740
of this bundle being pulled up.

00:36:20.740 --> 00:36:21.850
So this is one version.

00:36:21.850 --> 00:36:23.020
That's another version.

00:36:23.020 --> 00:36:25.450
And if you have multiple
assets, then I'll

00:36:25.450 --> 00:36:28.030
have multiple histories.

00:36:28.030 --> 00:36:31.460
Can this setup be
done in AWS as well?

00:36:31.460 --> 00:36:33.280
I'm not sure what that
means by this setup.

00:36:33.280 --> 00:36:38.120
But all of our tools can be
built on-prem or in the cloud.

00:36:38.120 --> 00:36:41.530
And this exact setup that
